 "provenance": {
  "oracle": "YAeHMOP bind 3.1.0b2 (built from source on lenovo)",
  "why": "the 3d basis: Si, P, S and Cl carry ICON8 3d parameters, so this is the only fixture that exercises s-d, p-d and d-d overlaps",
  "parameters": "s/p from Alvarez (eht_parms.dat as shipped); 3d from ICON8 (QCPE 517) BLOCK DATA, injected into a copy of the table (/tmp/eht_parms_d.dat) and handed to bind with BIND_PARM_FILE, so BOTH SIDES use identical numbers (P 3d -7.0/1.400, Cl 3d -9.0/2.033)",
  "k": 1.75,
  "hij": "nonweighted (Hoffmann plain form)",
  "frame": "the app example geometry ALIGNED to its principal axes; PCl5 is a trigonal bipyramid, so its frame is well conditioned",
  "note": "bind prints the UPPER triangle of S and leaves the rest zero; the matrix here is mirrored from it. Matrices print to 4 decimals, so the comparison floor is ~2e-4 in S (measured 1.07e-04) and ~0.05 eV in the highest virtuals (measured 0.035 eV), with the occupied ladder inside 0.002 eV (measured 0.001). The ORBITAL ORDER above is read off bind's own orbital mapping, not from the app (bind spells two of the d functions '3dx2y2' and '3z2'; the app prints '3dx2-y2' and '3dz2').",
  "generated": "2026-09-30"
 },
